{
  "description": "E213 paired indexed-cache controllers: A source-owner rounds, B disjoint closed-interval route phases. Identical stride-two nonadjacent graph, coefficients, features, resident route tables, ordered consumer and wire payload. C8/R3 minimum and C32/R5/K6/G3 packet-tail gates precede C8/R8/R16/R64/R128. ABBAAB repeats at R128; AB elsewhere. Complete immutable-input, numerical, counter and same-PE-clock audit follows every run. The R3 middle owner performs only local work; all owners communicate remotely at R>=4. R128 is the current host-contract limit, not a measured hardware frontier. Shared-link crossing negative remains a host result; no training or whole-GNN speedup claim.",
